From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:11:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_tristar: restart the USB hold on
 reconnect

Refresh the USB hold timestamp on every empty-input observation. A cable
reinserted after a long unplug must finish identification before data is
enabled. Keep the bounded fallback for persistent transitional states.
This applies to every board using the charger, including iPad 6.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index 6a9842eba..6e8e8368a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -1031,6 +1031,8 @@ static void tristar_poll(struct work_struct *work)
 	}
 	chg->online = status != 0;
 	if (!status) {
+		/* Identification starts after the empty period, not at unplug. */
+		chg->usb_off_ns = now;
 		if (chg->present) {
 			tristar_set_usb(chg, false);
 			chg->present = false;
